{"slug":"/students/subjects/biology/foundations/cell-properties/","source":"students/subjects/biology/foundations/cell-properties.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Cell Properties - Biology","description":"","subject":"biology","body":"<nav class=\"bg-white shadow-sm fixed top-0 w-full z-50\">\n        <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between h-16 items-center\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n                    <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/foundations/\" class=\"text-green-600 hover:text-green-800 mr-4\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span></a>\n                    <h1 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900\">Cell Properties &amp; Functions</h1>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 hidden sm:block\">Progress: <span id=\"progressPercent\">0%</span></div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <main class=\"pt-20 pb-8 px-4 max-w-5xl mx-auto\">\n        <div class=\"bg-green-50 border-l-4 border-green-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Describe the properties of cells and cellular processes</li>\n                <li>• Explain diffusion, osmosis, and active transport</li>\n                <li>• Understand cell specialization and differentiation</li>\n                <li>• Describe levels of organization in living organisms</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 1: Cell Properties -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n                Basic Properties of Cells\n            </h2>\n            \n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">All living cells share certain properties that distinguish them from non-living matter. These properties are essential for life.</p>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -circle-nodes mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Life Processes (MRS GREN)</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>M</strong>ovement - Cells can move substances</li>\n                        <li><strong>R</strong>espiration - Release energy from food</li>\n                        <li><strong>S</strong>ensitivity - Respond to stimuli</li>\n                        <li><strong>G</strong>rowth - Increase in size/number</li>\n                        <li><strong>R</strong>eproduction - Produce offspring</li>\n                        <li><strong>E</strong>xcretion - Remove waste products</li>\n                        <li><strong>N</strong>utrition - Obtain and use nutrients</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -dna mr-2\" data-mi=\"biotech\">biotech</span>Cell Theory</h4>\n                    <ol class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1 list-decimal list-inside\">\n                        <li>All living things are made of cells</li>\n                        <li>The cell is the basic unit of life</li>\n                        <li>All cells come from pre-existing cells</li>\n                    </ol>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-2\">Proposed by Schleiden, Schwann, and Virchow</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 2: Transport Across Cell Membrane -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n                Transport Across Cell Membrane\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The cell membrane is <strong>selectively permeable</strong> - it controls what enters and leaves the cell. There are three main types of transport:</p>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -arrows-alt-h mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>1. Diffusion</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The movement of particles from a <strong>region of higher concentration to lower concentration</strong>. Passive process (no energy required).</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm\"><strong>Examples:</strong> Oxygen entering cells, CO₂ leaving cells, perfume spreading in a room</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">Factors affecting rate: Concentration gradient, temperature, surface area, distance</p>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -tint mr-2\" data-mi=\"water_drop\">water_drop</span>2. Osmosis</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The movement of <strong>water molecules</strong> from a region of higher water potential (dilute solution) to lower water potential (concentrated solution) through a selectively permeable membrane.</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm\"><strong>Effects on cells:</strong></p>\n                        <ul class=\"text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1 space-y-1\">\n                            <li>• <strong>Hypotonic solution:</strong> Water enters → Cell swells/bursts (animal), becomes turgid (plant)</li>\n                            <li>• <strong>Hypertonic solution:</strong> Water leaves → Cell shrinks (crenates)</li>\n                            <li>• <strong>Isotonic solution:</strong> No net movement → Cell stays same</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -battery-full mr-2\" data-mi=\"battery_full\">battery_full</span>3. Active Transport</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The movement of particles from <strong>lower to higher concentration</strong> (against concentration gradient). Requires <strong>energy (ATP)</strong> and carrier proteins.</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                        <p class=\"text-sm\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n                        <ul class=\"text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1 space-y-1\">\n                            <li>• Root hair cells absorbing minerals from soil</li>\n                            <li>• Intestine cells absorbing glucose</li>\n                            <li>• Nerve cells pumping Na⁺/K⁺ ions</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-lg mt-4\">\n                <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n                    <thead>\n                        <tr class=\"border-b\">\n                            <th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Feature</th>\n                            <th class=\"p-2 text-center\">Diffusion</th>\n                            <th class=\"p-2 text-center\">Osmosis</th>\n                            <th class=\"p-2 text-center\">Active Transport</th>\n                        </tr>\n                    </thead>\n                    <tbody>\n                        <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Direction</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">High → Low</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">High → Low</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">Low → High</td></tr>\n                        <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Energy needed?</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">No</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">No</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">Yes (ATP)</td></tr>\n                        <tr><td class=\"p-2\">What moves?</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">Any particles</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">Water only</td><td class=\"p-2 text-center\">Ions/molecules</td></tr>\n                    </tbody>\n                </table>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 3: Cell Specialization -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n                Cell Specialization\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\"><strong>Differentiated cells</strong> are cells that have developed special structures to perform specific functions. The structure of a cell is always related to its function.</p>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 text-center mb-2\">Red Blood Cell</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Shape:</strong> Biconcave disc</li>\n                        <li><strong>Feature:</strong> No nucleus</li>\n                        <li><strong>Function:</strong> Transport oxygen</li>\n                        <li><strong>Adaptation:</strong> Large surface area for gas exchange</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 text-center mb-2\">Root Hair Cell</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Shape:</strong> Long extension</li>\n                        <li><strong>Feature:</strong> Thin wall, large vacuole</li>\n                        <li><strong>Function:</strong> Absorb water/minerals</li>\n                        <li><strong>Adaptation:</strong> Large surface area for absorption</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 text-center mb-2\">Muscle Cell</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Shape:</strong> Elongated, cylindrical</li>\n                        <li><strong>Feature:</strong> Many mitochondria</li>\n                        <li><strong>Function:</strong> Contraction &amp; movement</li>\n                        <li><strong>Adaptation:</strong> Contains protein fibers for contraction</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 text-center mb-2\">Nerve Cell (Neuron)</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Shape:</strong> Long axon with branches</li>\n                        <li><strong>Feature:</strong> Myelin sheath</li>\n                        <li><strong>Function:</strong> Transmit impulses</li>\n                        <li><strong>Adaptation:</strong> Long to connect distant parts</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-700 text-center mb-2\">Sperm Cell</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Shape:</strong> Head, midpiece, tail</li>\n                        <li><strong>Feature:</strong> Many mitochondria in midpiece</li>\n                        <li><strong>Function:</strong> Fertilize egg</li>\n                        <li><strong>Adaptation:</strong> Tail for swimming to egg</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-pink-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-pink-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-pink-700 text-center mb-2\">Palisade Cell</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-xs space-y-1\">\n                        <li><strong>Shape:</strong> Column-shaped</li>\n                        <li><strong>Feature:</strong> Many chloroplasts</li>\n                        <li><strong>Function:</strong> Photosynthesis</li>\n                        <li><strong>Adaptation:</strong> Packed with chloroplasts near light</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 4: Levels of Organization -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n                Levels of Organization\n            </h2>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Living organisms are organized in a hierarchy from simplest to most complex:</p>\n\n            <div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2 text-center mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 px-4 py-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"font-semibold text-green-700\">Cell</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Basic unit</p>\n                </div>\n                <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-gray-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-100 px-4 py-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700\">Tissue</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Similar cells</p>\n                </div>\n                <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-gray-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-100 px-4 py-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700\">Organ</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Tissues together</p>\n                </div>\n                <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-gray-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                <div class=\"bg-orange-100 px-4 py-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"font-semibold text-orange-700\">System</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Organs together</p>\n                </div>\n                <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-gray-400\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                <div class=\"bg-red-100 px-4 py-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"font-semibold text-red-700\">Organism</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Complete being</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2\">Examples:</h4>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                    <li><strong>Tissue:</strong> Muscle tissue, nervous tissue, xylem tissue</li>\n                    <li><strong>Organ:</strong> Heart, leaf, kidney, stomach</li>\n                    <li><strong>System:</strong> Circulatory system, digestive system, nervous system</li>\n                    <li><strong>Organism:</strong> Human, tree, bacteria</li>\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 5: Video -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n                Video: Cell Transport\n            </h2>\n            <div class=\"video-container bg-gray-100 rounded-lg\">\n                <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/os-HooAmMGo\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Practice -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-green-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>Practice Questions\n            </h2>\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Explain why red blood cells have no nucleus.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            Red blood cells have no nucleus to <strong>create more space for hemoglobin</strong>, the protein that carries oxygen. This allows each cell to carry more oxygen, making transport more efficient.\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. What is the difference between diffusion and active transport?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Diffusion:</strong> Movement from high to low concentration; no energy required; passive process.<br>\n                            <strong>Active transport:</strong> Movement from low to high concentration; requires ATP energy; uses carrier proteins.\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. What would happen to a red blood cell placed in pure water?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            Water would enter the cell by <strong>osmosis</strong> (from high water potential outside to lower water potential inside). The cell would swell and eventually <strong>burst (lyse)</strong> because it has no cell wall to prevent over-expansion.\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-emerald-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-green-200 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                <li>• Cells are the basic unit of life with properties like respiration, growth, reproduction</li>\n                <li>• Diffusion and osmosis are passive (no energy); Active transport requires ATP</li>\n                <li>• Cell structure is always related to function (specialization)</li>\n                <li>• Organization: Cell → Tissue → Organ → System → Organism</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center mt-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/foundations/cell-structure/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900\"><span class=\"mi -chevron-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_left\">chevron_left</span>Previous</a>\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/biology/foundations/classification/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 bg-green-500 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-green-600\">Next: Classification<span class=\"mi -chevron-right ml-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_right\">chevron_right</span></a>\n        </div>\n    </main>","bodyClass":"bg-gray-50 min-h-screen","bodyStyle":"","css":["@keyframes fade-in-up { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }\n        .animate-fade-in-up { animation: fade-in-up 0.5s ease-out forwards; }\n        .section-card { background: white; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; }\n        .video-container { position: relative; width: 100%; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 8px; }\n        .video-container iframe { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}